{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1050239-true-blood-conversion","id":1050239,"title":"True Blood Conversion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-16T19:19:43-08:00","id":1050239,"title":"True Blood Conversion","content":"A long, long time ago, I made a <i>True Blood </i>conversion for <b>Vampire</b>, mostly as a thought experiment. It's one of those things I occasionally return to and tweak, and I have a feeling I've posted an older version before in an unrelated thread.<br /> <br /> While <i>True Blood </i>hasn't been on the air for a while, and I'm really only a half-hearted fan (or at least I was before it got <i>really </i>wacky), I thought it might be fun to share with y'all. I don't actually think it's all that playable; I tried to stick with what the show presents about vampires, which admittedly is a bit contradictory. I don't know if it'd actually be all that fun to be this strict with the setting, rather than just hand waving it and using vanilla <b>Requiem</b>, which as far as a &quot;generic&quot; RPGs about vampires go, there're none better.<br /> <br /> Anyway, enjoy.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35eHBlQzA5N1plUkk/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E...ew?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-catego